# s6_per_layer: model converted, encrypted and run one sub-model at a time.
#
# admission  phase B step (2026-08-18), measured off-path first as x1_per_layer (different driver script;
#            not disqualifying under PROCEDURE.md). Conditions:
#            (a) transcript identical to the predecessor:
#                  s5_embed_chunk (whole model)   bytes=11,228,688,384   rounds=1525
#                  x1_per_layer   (decomposed)    bytes=11,228,688,384   rounds=1525
#                driver alone: x0_per_layer_base bytes=11,228,688,384 rounds=1495 = s0_default.
#            (b) impl/equiv_per_layer.py: "12 layers: decomposition is bit-identical to the whole model";
#                mask assumption checked against get_extended_attention_mask.
# order      s5_embed_chunk already phase B (evidence=equivalent, +30 rounds); phase B after phase B is allowed.
# reason     published peak = whole-model ONNX conversion; three 433 MB releases in that phase null
#            (off-path-runs/s6_conversion_phase/). Per-layer conversion removes the phase.
# expected   ~1,290,000 kB vs s5's 2,056,996 (-37%); transcript unchanged.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
